Ported modules (upstream path -> this package):

  src/utils/quota/parsers.ts (normalizers)
      -> src/normalize.ts
  src/utils/quota/resetInstants.ts
      -> src/reset-instants.ts
  src/utils/quota/builders.ts (buildAntigravityQuotaGroups, buildKimiQuotaRows,
     buildXaiBillingSummary window logic)
      -> src/windows-antigravity.ts, src/windows-kimi.ts, src/windows-xai.ts
  src/utils/quota/resetCredits.ts (normalizeCodexResetCreditsPayload)
      -> src/reset-credits.ts
  src/utils/quota/xaiPaid.ts (isPaidXaiAuthFile)
      -> src/xai-tier.ts
  src/features/quota/providers/claude/data.ts (buildClaudeQuotaWindows)
      -> src/windows-claude.ts
  src/features/quota/providers/codex/data.ts (buildCodexQuotaWindows)
      -> src/windows-codex.ts
  src/utils/quota/constants.ts (probe endpoints and request headers)
      -> src/windows-*.ts constants

Adaptations from upstream: i18next `TFunction` labels and SCSS/theme coupling
removed (window identity is a stable key); display-only formatting dropped;
missing counters are never defaulted to zero; the xAI paid health probe
(/v1/me plus chat completion) and the Codex reset-credit consume operation are
not ported — this package is read-only and never sends an inference request.

Further divergences required by this repository's review: Kimi label-keyword
period derivation and the unknown-unit minute default are dropped (a display
label is not a time basis); Codex windows without `limit_window_seconds` keep
positional `primary`/`secondary` keys instead of claiming 5-hour/weekly
periods; an xAI payload whose period carries no quota counter produces no
window; a non-array `credits` field is a shape violation rather than a zero
count; response bounds are byte-exact (UTF-8) and also cover already-decoded
bodies; and one observation retains at most 256 windows.

